# The whole build context is packed and sent to the docker daemon BEFORE the first instruction of
# the Dockerfile runs, so everything named here is time and bandwidth saved on every single build.
# Without this file that transfer includes .venv alone at ~65 MB — a host-built virtualenv holding
# macOS/arm64 wheels for a Python 3.14 that does not exist in python:3.11-slim.
#
# It is also a second line of defence rather than the only one. The Dockerfile copies exactly three
# paths (main.py, src/, static/) instead of `COPY . .`, so nothing below could reach the image today
# anyway. That is precisely why this file has to exist: the day someone writes `COPY . .` — the
# single most common edit a Dockerfile ever receives — this is what keeps the git history, the
# developer's local .venv, the runtime data/ directory and the CI machinery out of a published
# image.
#
# PART of that is checked rather than assumed, and it is worth knowing exactly which part.
# ci/smoke.py's in-image probe asserts that /app/.venv, /app/.git, /app/tests and /app/ci are
# ABSENT from the built artefact, and that /app/data is EMPTY — emptiness and not absence, because
# the Dockerfile creates that directory deliberately so a mounted volume inherits its ownership.
# `.env` is NOT on that list, and leaving it off is the deliberate choice: the file is gitignored
# and only `make env` creates it, so the CI checkout the gate runs against never has one and such a
# row would pass without ever having been able to fail. What actually keeps a developer's `.env`
# out of a published image is the three explicit COPY lines above — and this file, on the day
# somebody replaces them with `COPY . .`.

# Version control and CI machinery: never needed at runtime, and .git in particular carries the
# whole history of the repository into a public registry image.
.git
.gitignore
.gitea
.github
ci/

# Host-built virtualenvs. Wrong interpreter, wrong platform, ~65 MB.
.venv/
venv/

# Bytecode compiled by a different interpreter than the one in the image.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Runtime state. `data/` exists on a workstation and holds a developer's real streams.json —
# including MQTT and InfluxDB passwords. It must never be baked into an image; in production the
# state directory is a docker volume mounted at run time (see docker-compose.yml).
data/

# The developer's own environment, created by `make env`. src/settings.py names `.env` in its
# SettingsConfigDict, so pydantic-settings reads it wherever it finds one. A real environment
# variable still wins over the file — but every variable the deployment does NOT set would then come
# from a workstation's copy instead of from the defaults in src/settings.py, and `.env.example` ships
# `DATA_DIR=./data`. Baked in at /app/.env that is a container writing its whole configuration to a
# relative path in the image's writable layer, which the next update deletes.
.env

# Tests and their fixtures are run in CI from the source tree, not from the image.
tests/
pytest.ini
requirements-dev.txt

# Documentation, editor and deploy files: read by humans and by the deploy host, not by the app.
*.md
Makefile
docker-compose.yml
*.code-workspace
.roo/
.DS_Store
